# Database

- Runtime driver is always `pg` (`src/db/connection.ts`), including Neon TCP.
  Do not switch routes to `@neondatabase/serverless` HTTP — no transactions
  (`db.transaction()` is used by ingest and folder moves).
- Schema is `src/db/schema/index.ts` (plus `auth.ts`). After edits:
  `pnpm db:generate`, commit the SQL, rely on `pnpm db:migrate` (Vercel
  `vercel:build` does this). Do not `drizzle-kit push` on production.
- Local Docker force-push: `pnpm db:local:push`. Interactive `pnpm db:push`
  fails without a TTY.
- `pnpm db:ensure-workspace-users` is Neon HTTP. Skip it against Docker.
- Expression indexes must match query SQL byte-for-byte (English FTS on
  `document_chunks.contextual_text`). `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY` cannot run
  inside Drizzle’s transactional migrator.
- Attachment tables: `reportAttachments`, `attachmentIngestRuns`,
  `documentPages`, `documentChunks` (pgvector 768). Soft-delete via
  `deletedAt`; retrieval joins `activeIngestRunId`.
- Product History: `documentRevisions` + `documentRevisionSections` (one
  snapshot per Agent-chrome report turn). Do not reuse
  `sectionContentVersions` for that UI — the audit table records every PATCH
  including human autosave. Worksheet writes are not document versions.
